My feeling is that glibc upstream will not want to care about cross qemu
situations. I would prefer to report it to the Ubuntu cross-tools
maintainers: The package libc6-<cpu>-cross contains the file /usr/<cpu
>-linux-gnu/lib/libc.so.6; they could surely add the symlink for
/usr/<cpu>-linux-gnu/etc/ld.so.cache as well.

-- =

